WEBVTT

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:55.010
The Strongest Stalker

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.720
Time for breakfast, princess...

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.650
Oh, boy.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:15.520
Whoa, Sisi...

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:16.940
I know, I know.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:19.670
I haven't forgotten yours, okay?

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:21.980
Here.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:23.840
Did you sleep well?

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:24.080
Here.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:27.800
Not very.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:32.290
You need to do something about the 
household items Cardia uses, and soon.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:34.710
On the double with a pillow, especially.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.080
Utensils, too, please!

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.340
If you're only going to eat sandwiches,

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:44.710
Impey the genius chef 
can't show off his skills!

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:48.980
The sandwiches you made for dinner
 last night were so delicious, though.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.340
I was surprised to learn 
what a good cook you are.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:55.930
Cardia! You really are an angel!

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:57.000
Marry me!

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.050
If you touch me, you'll melt.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:59.190
Whoa...

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.480
Well, love is never without its obstacles.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.520
You all sound more lively 
than usual this morning.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.370
Saint?

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:10.080
You're back?

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:11.920
Saint?

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:15.450
There's one other guy, Saint, but...

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.620
I'm sure he'll show up sooner or later.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.200
Welcome to my mansion.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:26.250
I'm Saint-Germain.
 A pleasure to meet you, Cardia.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:30.900
I have been waiting for you for a very long time.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.060
Waiting... for me?

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.020
Hey! No hitting on Cardia!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.770
Like you're one to talk.

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.780
Saint is a guy with weird taste.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:52.600
He does a lot to support us.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.450
Nobility is just so boring.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:55.900
Right, right!

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:59.200
He's so bored, he even takes in terrorists!

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.040
I told you, I was framed!

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:08.800
Oh, I used to work for the 
government as a researcher.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:11.770
He was the Head Royal Alchemist.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.920
An elite among elites, basically.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:18.100
I'm no elite anymore, though. 
Now I'm on the run from the government.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.450
Did you quit? Why?

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.190
Well...

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:34.200
Well, everyone has a thing or two 
that they don't want to talk about!

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.730
More importantly, what are we gonna do now?

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:44.330
The first phase, getting the Horologium 
away from Twilight, was successful.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:45.840
So, next...

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:50.700
I think our best option is to lie low 
 and gather information on them.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.480
Isn't there a way to make things go faster?

00:04:54.970 --> 00:04:57.310
Like capturing Twilight's leader!

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:00.350
Tell 'em to cut out the terrorism,
 and slug 'em a good one!

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:03.850
I'm not sure we have the strength 
between us to get away with that.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:06.150
We'll start with what we're sure we can do.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:10.700
Fortunately, we have the princess, 
and she can give us some clues.

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:20.880
What a disappointment.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.880
I can't believe you let some 
petty thief snatch our prey.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.870
How far the Royal Family's
 personal guard has fallen.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:30.520
Don't you agree with me,

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:32.610
Your Majesty?

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:36.710
If you had disclosed more accurate
 information about the monster,

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:38.770
this would never have happened.

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:40.890
Do you not agree,

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:44.130
Finis, leader of Twilight?

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:49.910
Listen to you! Isn't keeping 
secrets your forte?

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:54.340
While London prospers, so many 
have shed blood in the shadows...

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:57.030
Both humans, and those not quite human.

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:03.040
How many filthy, unspeakable jobs
 do you think we've accepted for you?

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.800
In any case...

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:11.770
You can forget about this mission.

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:15.820
We have our soldiers on
 the move to reclaim our prey.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:20.680
Are you saying you set those 
ghastly men of yours loose in my city?

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:26.040
If your dogs hadn't screwed up,
 I wouldn't have had to do a thing.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.210
Why don't you all have a meeting 
to discuss your failure later?

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:31.440
Finis.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:36.020
You may think you have me 
at your beck and call,

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.890
but as you were born in this country,

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:40.700
you are still my precious child.

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:45.700
When a child takes his mischief too far, 
it's a mother's job to punish him.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.850
Do remember that.

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:03.520
Thanks.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:06.730
Well, Fran? Did you figure anything out?

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:07.660
Yeah.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:12.530
As we thought, the poison in Cardia's
 body is a result of the Horologium.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:15.580
Can't you remove it from her body?

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:16.910
I...

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.570
can't recommend that.

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:22.580
I sort of predicted this, but...

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.080
Cardia, I don't hear a heartbeat.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:32.360
It's possible that your heart
 itself has been lost.

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:35.120
I have... no heart?

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:40.880
What keeps you alive is, without a doubt,
 the eternally-beating heart...

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:43.350
the Horologium itself.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:46.310
It functions as your heart.

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:53.820
Okay, then!

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:56.330
Cardia, let's go to town.

00:07:56.770 --> 00:07:58.040
Now?

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:00.660
No time like the present, as they say.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:34.500
Please proceed,

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.170
Baron Gilford Dudley and party.

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:47.670
Well done!

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.950
Is it okay to take those off?

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:52.290
We're safe once we pass inspection.

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:55.040
The Yard is probably 
short-staffed right now,

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.970
what with all those thefts
 targeting noble households lately.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:02.520
Oh, that flashy thief, right?

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:04.520
It's not me.

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:07.270
Well, this is my stop.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:09.190
You're not coming with us?

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:11.770
There's something I want to pick up.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:13.730
Let's go, Impey.

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:16.000
What?! I wanna stay with Cardia—

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.530
You promised to help me, didn't you?

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:23.800
Well, then, shall we treat 
ourselves to a date?

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.910
Date?

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:32.470
There are so many people,
 both inside and outside the gate.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:35.720
Did my father really commit
 terrorist acts in this town?

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:39.020
Yeah, sadly, there's no doubt about it.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:43.710
What if... What if a terrorist 
attack were to happen?

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:46.610
A lot of people would die.

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:47.690
That's why

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:49.580
we have to stop it from happening.

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:54.940
Anyway!

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:58.280
Next, I'll show you the busiest place in London!

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.520
This is a casino?

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:18.370
Oh, you know about them?

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:21.840
I read about them in books. 
People come here to get more money.

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:24.450
Money isn't all you get here, though.

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.760
This casino is an underground trade show.

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.370
All sorts of info flies around.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.560
Gathering information?

00:10:31.090 --> 00:10:33.040
Was I in the way?

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:34.060
In the way?

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.930
Since I can't do anything...

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:40.080
I can't talk like you, Lupin.

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:48.700
A chatty Cardia would be an amusing sight,
 but don't worry about that.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:53.040
We're just here today because I thought
 it'd be a nice change of pace for you.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:55.690
Why are you doing all this for me?

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:56.520
Huh?

00:10:56.900 --> 00:11:00.900
You, Fran, and Impey are very kind to me.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.410
But I...

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:08.640
You saw Sisi's leg, right?

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:15.010
Apparently, some complete 
stranger lopped it off.

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:19.170
Impey brought him home, 
saying he felt sorry for him,

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:21.470
and made that prosthetic leg, 
bawling all the while.

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:24.930
His love is still one-sided, though.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:29.050
But Sisi is still alive because of that.

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:31.340
He loves his food, too.

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:33.930
It's the same for you.

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:37.430
So what if you have 
no heart? You're still alive.

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:40.340
You're no different from us.

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:41.790
Right?

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:45.040
Yeah.

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:47.810
Besides...

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:52.760
A heart doesn't <i>really</i> start beating 
until you find the person you love.

00:11:52.760 --> 00:11:53.440
Huh?

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:56.660
Whether you're a man or a woman, 
when you truly fall in love,

00:11:56.660 --> 00:11:58.820
you want to touch the one you love.

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:02.230
When you feel their warmth,

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:05.320
this starts to beat.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:15.520
I want to touch...

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:16.710
Huh?

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:20.350
You said you would grant my wish.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:24.980
I want to touch you.

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:27.840
I want to feel your warmth.

00:12:28.300 --> 00:12:32.410
Er, that... sure is a pick-up line...

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:34.340
Pick-up...

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:36.730
Never mind.

00:12:39.310 --> 00:12:40.900
Understood.

00:12:41.300 --> 00:12:43.640
On my name, Arsène Lupin,

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:47.100
I swear that I shall grant your wish.

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:51.700
I'll save the kiss until then.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:57.550
Lupin?

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:02.100
Cardia, we're leaving.

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:27.140
Beautiful women are the best!

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:29.230
I'm back.

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:43.460
Twilight!

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:50.720
What?

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:51.970
They're gone?!

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:11.980
They flanked us, huh?

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:35.500
Don't move.

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:39.520
They're rock salt shells, 
but still hurt if they hit,

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:41.180
Arsène Lupin.

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:44.300
Have we met, pretty boy?

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:46.480
Not that you're as pretty as me.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:49.320
Give me the monster.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:54.680
I know you snatched
 Twilight's prey from them.

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:56.530
Just hand it over.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.500
Sorry, but I never stole any monster.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:04.700
Wait.

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:06.880
The monster you speak of is me.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:08.690
Don't hurt Lupin.

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:09.990
Hey, Cardia!

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:13.010
You're... the monster?

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:15.700
Both of you, get down!

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:21.270
Let's go!

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:22.650
Hurry!

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:23.840
Thanks for the help.

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:25.890
Cardia, I'll— whoa!

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.080
It's easier to run this way.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:31.590
You...

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:34.370
Jeez... Just don't trip!

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:53.710
Get in! Quick!

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:57.330
Did we get away?

00:15:57.330 --> 00:15:58.730
Don't let your guard down.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:02.440
Not only did he know of me, 
he also put out a net.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:05.070
I wouldn't put it past him 
to know our escape route.

00:16:05.530 --> 00:16:08.230
If anyone could, it'd be him.

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:09.150
Huh?

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.560
Fran, do you know that man?

00:16:11.560 --> 00:16:14.780
Yeah. I saw him when I lived at the palace.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:15.990
The palace?

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:34.760
Are you all right, Cardia?

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.720
Yes, I'm fine.

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:47.060
Lupin! Cardia!

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:48.260
I'm sure of it now.

00:16:48.660 --> 00:16:50.990
He used to be a member of Twilight.

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:53.590
They called him the "human weapon"...

00:16:53.590 --> 00:16:55.970
Abraham Van Helsing.

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:58.070
Woman.

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:01.630
What do they mean when
 they call you a monster?

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:06.550
Do you have those jewels, the Horologium?

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:17.180
I am Cardia, daughter of Isaac Beckford.

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:20.230
You're Isaac's daughter?

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:25.320
I see. You'll make good bait.

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:26.740
Van.

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:32.770
It sounds like you want to use her to
 make some kind of deal with Twilight.

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:35.130
What are you really after?

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:39.170
I have only one target.

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:42.030
The leader of Twilight, Finis.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:45.330
I'll have him dragged before me

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:49.150
and make him pay for the unforgivable
 atrocities he's committed.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.520
And this woman...

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:55.200
is a necessary pawn in my plan.

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:00.050
In that case, there's a better way.

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.560
Work with us.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:03.530
Huh?!

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:04.720
What did you say?

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:07.470
If you consider both of our objectives,

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:10.750
working together should benefit 
you as much as it would us.

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:14.480
H-Hang on, Fran! What are you saying?!

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:17.480
Yeah, that might be wise.

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:18.560
Huh?!

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:22.480
Even if we escape today, 
it won't change anything.

00:18:22.480 --> 00:18:25.170
But if you're on our side,

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:27.930
we'll have a powerful force 
to go up against Twilight.

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:30.110
Isn't it win-win?

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:32.920
I see... Wait, really?

00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:35.450
What do you say?

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:38.050
I refuse.

00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:40.740
Talking any longer is a waste of time.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.730
Come, woman.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:47.970
Lupin...

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:54.450
I can't trust some rude jerk who'd 
decline our gracious invitation

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:57.730
to escort a lady anywhere.

00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:00.000
Have it your way.

00:19:00.670 --> 00:19:01.250
Don't—

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:16.260
Lupin?

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:18.040
Lupin!

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:23.290
"Lupin's Magic," I call it.

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:27.340
You... rigged my gun?

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:30.020
Want me to reveal the secret of my magic?

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:35.280
I put adhesive putty on a ball
 I stole from the casino

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:37.030
and stuffed it in the muzzle of your gun.

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:39.070
But when did you do that?

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:43.670
While my very perceptive assistant
 was talking up a storm.

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:49.750
I was serious about the offer, though.

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:54.000
Our goal is to stop Twilight's plot,

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.940
but unfortunately, we lack
 the force to stand against them.

00:19:58.410 --> 00:19:59.890
You're very honest.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:04.630
But how would I benefit 
from becoming your sword?

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:07.350
If you join us,

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:09.900
we'll be able to pull off 
some daring operations.

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:13.270
And the more our enemy comes to despise us,

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:15.460
the thicker our red thread of fate grows.

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:17.160
I guarantee it.

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:20.290
Finis will, without a doubt, 
show himself to us.

00:20:21.390 --> 00:20:22.550
I'll ask again.

00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:24.600
Let's work together.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:29.720
Fine.

00:20:30.280 --> 00:20:34.310
I'll take you up on that, 
Victor Frankenstein.

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:37.290
Huh? Y-You know my...

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:42.540
How could I not know the former
 Head Royal Alchemist?

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:50.180
So, um... Can we say that's 
one matter resolved for now?

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:52.580
So he'll be one of us now?

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:56.400
Yeah, I hope so, at least.

00:20:57.400 --> 00:21:00.240
But he's got some complicated motivations.

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:06.800
<i>I feel like his cold eyes 
could hold me prisoner,</i>

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:10.850
<i>because I saw a sad color in their depths.</i>

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:13.980
<i>Why is he crying?</i>

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:17.360
<i>What is he hiding in his heart?</i>

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:57.360
I knew we could count on you!

00:22:57.360 --> 00:23:00.580
Now I can really show 
off my cooking skills!

00:23:00.880 --> 00:23:02.660
Thank you, Fran.

00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:06.720
You're welcome. Now... may I?

00:23:07.240 --> 00:23:10.510
I wonder how this cloth was made...

00:23:10.510 --> 00:23:13.070
The material's normal, so it's not the textile.

00:23:13.070 --> 00:23:15.330
Is something coating the surface?

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:16.190
Hey!

00:23:16.190 --> 00:23:17.080
Huh?

00:23:17.550 --> 00:23:20.460
Oh! S-Sorry! I didn't mean any harm!

00:23:21.740 --> 00:23:23.120
I don't mind.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:30.370
Looks like one more red thread

00:23:31.070 --> 00:23:33.670
has become tangled around him now...
